  # continuing past #26/#27): a NEGATIVE fixnum reaching this slow path
  # (it already failed the fast path's top-16-bit check above, since a
  # negative fixnum's sign-extension sets those bits) has a FAMILY
  # NIBBLE of all-ones (0xF) here -- matching NEITHER 0 (the ordinary
  # fixnum case) NOR NUMERIC_FAMILY (BigInt, 0x1) below, so it fell
  # through to .DYN_OBJ_'s generic identity-only dispatch, where
  # ordering comparisons (`<`/`<=`/`>`/`>=`) are hardcoded to always
  # return false. Confirmed exactly: `open_i < 0` with open_i = -1,
  # inside a dynamic-mode function, silently evaluated to false.
  #
